  "help_title": "CLI Reference — SimpleLog",
  "help_content": "USAGE\n  simplelog [OPTIONS] [FILE ...]\n  command | simplelog [OPTIONS]\n\nARGUMENTS\n  FILE ...          One or more log file paths.\n\nOPTIONS\n  --split MODE      How to open logs on startup.\n                    tab (default) | vertical | horizontal\n  --tail N          Lines to load from the end of each file (default: 100).\n\nKEYBOARD SHORTCUTS\n  Ctrl+F            Focus sidebar search\n  Ctrl+Shift+F      Toggle sidebar\n\nEXAMPLES\n  simplelog\n  simplelog /var/log/syslog\n  simplelog --tail 500 /var/log/nginx/access.log\n  simplelog --split vertical app.log error.log\n  journalctl -f | simplelog\n  kubectl logs -f my-pod | simplelog\n  docker logs -f my-container | simplelog\n",
